Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:44:36 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 220/230] test(matchCardCenter): portable browser path, real
 screenshot helper, direct-invocation guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Replace hard-coded Windows chrome.exe path with: CHROMIUM_PATH env var,
  else chromium.executablePath() (Playwright bundled), else SKIPPED.
- Replace stale card.screenshotEl.screenshot() (cannot work on serialized
  objects from $$eval) with page.locator('li.list-in > a').nth(i).screenshot().
- Refactor to export runMatchCardCenterTests() for measurement-only runners
  and re-export VIEWPORTS, TEST_CASES locally (no barrel re-export — the
  import-from-sibling form broke esbuild with duplicate export names).
- Direct-invocation guard via import.meta.url === new URL('file://' + ...).
- Add an audit comment: src/lib/telegram.ts does NOT set
  --tg-safe-area-inset-top or --tg-content-safe-area-inset-top; the only
  --safe-* definitions live in html[data-embed="1"]. Inside Telegram,
  .pad-safe-top resolves to max(env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px), 8px), so
  absent a notch or Telegram inset the header gap is already exactly 8px.
